<!--
  sitemap.xml for fellowscript.com (task 20260909-website-seo)

  Domain note (Configuration Q2/Q7): this file lives under frontend/public/,
  which Vite copies byte-for-byte into dist/ with no templating; it can't
  consume the VITE_SITE_URL build-time env var the way React-rendered
  <head> tags do (see src/config.js's SITE_URL and src/components/Seo.jsx).
  The literal domain below is this file's single authoring source, not a
  value hand-duplicated from elsewhere.

  HashRouter limitation (see the Decision comment near HashRouter in
  frontend/src/App.jsx): only "/" is a genuinely distinct, server-resolvable
  URL today. Only genuinely public, unauthenticated routes are listed here
  (Security Posture Q2).

  Task 20260918-fix-google-indexing-audit (Issue B / option B1): this file
  used to also list https://fellowscript.com/#/privacy and .../#/terms as a
  best-effort, forward-compatible declaration. They were removed: under
  HashRouter, everything after "#" is a client-side fragment the server
  never sees, so those were never independently crawlable/indexable URLs,
  just dead sitemap entries. There is no real static-route equivalent to
  point them at instead (confirmed as of this task), so removal was the
  applicable fix per the report's own B1 option, not a repoint. They can be
  re-added, pointing at real paths, if this project ever migrates off
  HashRouter.
-->
